<div class="blurb aboutus">
<div class="header"><h1>About bbsengine</h1></div>
<div class="body">
<p>bbsengine is an open source (GPLv2+) application platform. It
primarily uses text interfaces with a web version available. The
project was started around 2002 and has evolved through several
major revisions: bbsengine3, bbsengine4, bbsengine5, and the
current bbsengine6.</p>

<h2>What it does</h2>
<p>bbsengine has been used to build office applications
("projectflow") as well as games ("empyre" for starters). It
provides ANSI escape sequence support for vt102 / ECMA-48
terminals, a structured input layer, and a session/member
abstraction layer that backs both text-mode BBS doors and a web
frontend.</p>

<h2>How it's organized</h2>
<p>The engine ships as a per-vhost <code>/engine/</code> install
(<code>engine/router.php</code>, <code>engine/serve-md.php</code>,
<code>engine/join.php</code>, ...) backed by PHP Smarty templates
under <code>skin/tmpl/</code>. The handbook at
<code>/handbook/6/</code> is the canonical spec tree and is
rendered live by the same router via
<code>page-markdown.tmpl</code>.</p>

<h2>How do I get it?</h2>
<p>There are no public downloads of bbsengine6 available at this
time. The source tree is maintained in the project's internal
git repository.</p>
</div>
